        "department": null,
        "description": "\"Correlation is not causation\" is a familiar phrase. Then what is causation? This course attempts to answer this question. The recent literature has seen advances in identifying causal paramaters using both experiemental and observational data. This course will walk students through these methods, the situations under which they may be applied; their strengths and limitations. In each case, an empirical application, pertaining to India, that uses the method will discussed; so as to anchor theory with application.",
        "prerequisites_mandatory": [
            "Econometrics I or Statistical Inference"
        ],
        "prerequisites_desirable": [
            "Familiarity with either Stata or R",
            "Microeconomics"
        ],
        "prerequisites_mandatory_resolved": [
            "Econometrics I or Statistical Inference"
        ],
        "prerequisites_desirable_resolved": [
            "Familiarity with either Stata or R",
            "Microeconomics"
        ]
    },
